Yashichi <devnull@127.0.0.1> writes:
> Counterpoint question: how do you *remove* a name from something? Leaving
> the field empty when trying to rename just leaves the original.

>From the Guidebook (which Raisse quite rightly advises reading in the
article you're following up to):

  The command `C' allows you to assign a name to a monster, which may
  be useful to help distinguish one from another when multiple
  monsters are present.  Assigning a name which is just a space will
  remove any prior name.

  When you use ``#name'' on an object which has already been named,
  specifying a space as the value will remove the prior name instead
  of assigning a new one.

